# scenarios/2_vat.books: loaded by ledger_server into 2_vat.db the first time it is picked,
# and again by Start over. Amounts are in cents.
title	2. VAT: collected for the tax office, not earned
about	The VAT paid on a purchase is claimed back (VAT to recover), the VAT charged on a sale is owed (VAT to pay); neither is a cost or a revenue. At the VAT return the two are set off, and the bank pays the difference.
about	Try it: record a purchase with 21% VAT, and see where the VAT goes.
currency	USD
account	100000	equity	Capital
account	550000	asset	Bank account
account	240000	asset	Furniture
account	411000	asset	VAT to recover
account	700000	revenue	Sales
account	400001	asset	Customer 1
account	451000	liability	VAT to pay
entry	2011-01-02	The founder puts in savings
posting	Capital	-1000000
posting	Bank account	1000000
entry	2011-01-10	A desk for 1,000 (21% VAT)
posting	Bank account	-121000
posting	Furniture	100000
posting	VAT to recover	21000
entry	2011-02-01	Consulting invoiced to customer 1 for 2,000 (21% VAT)
posting	Sales	-200000
posting	VAT to pay	-42000
posting	Customer 1	242000
entry	2011-02-28	Customer 1 pays, VAT included
posting	Customer 1	-242000
posting	Bank account	242000
entry	2011-04-20	The VAT return: 420 owed less 210 to recover, the bank pays 210
posting	VAT to recover	-21000
posting	Bank account	-21000
posting	VAT to pay	42000
